        <mxCell id="c200" value="&lt;i&gt;The PivotTable is filtered to FiscalYear 2026, sorted from the largest Sum of Amount, with the second Sum of Amount shown as % Running Total In, named Running share of spending. Outlined: the row where the share first reaches 50 percent, supplier 19 of 103 (coral). Selected: F7, which counts the suppliers below 50 percent and adds one; F8 and F9 do the same for 80 and 90 percent, and the three marks are outlined (teal). With the filter left on all years the marks read 22, 60 and 78. E10 to F12 (the largest supplier) are not shown.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="696" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
